# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How to add your keys
#   1. Copy this file to a new file named  .env  (same folder as server.py):
#        Windows (PowerShell):  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#        Mac / Linux:           cp .env.example .env
#   2. Open .env and paste each key after the "=" sign. No quotes, no spaces
#      around the key, and nothing after it on the same line.
#   3. Restart the app:  python server.py
#   4. Never share or commit .env. It is already listed in .gitignore.
#   5. On Vercel, .env is not uploaded. Add the same names and values under
#      Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables, then redeploy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Gemini key for the chat model and the note embeddings.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey  (Create API key)
gemini_api_key=

# Optional. The chat model name. The app currently uses gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# (set in config.py), so you can leave this as it is.
gemini_modoel=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# Optional, needed only if you deploy to Vercel. Keeps your uploaded notes
# permanent. In the Vercel dashboard open Storage -> Create -> Blob, connect it
# to your project, then copy the token Vercel shows. Without it, notes stay on
# your own computer only.
STUDY_STORAGE_STORE_ID=
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# Optional. Voice typing (the mic button), works locally and on Vercel.
# Get a key at https://console.deepgram.com  ->  API Keys  ->  Create a New API Key.
#   - Any key works: the mic records short pieces and shows the words every few seconds.
#   - A key with the "Member" role or higher also unlocks true live typing (words appear as you speak).
# Needs localhost or HTTPS (browsers block the microphone elsewhere).
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
